in @code
in @prism
in @glass
in @meta
in @nl

# @code/mirror — mirror's instance of @code at the mirror altitude.
#
# The recognition (2026-06-06, Reed + Alex → Mara): mirror IS code at
# the mirror altitude. Same as @code/rust IS code at the Rust altitude,
# @code/llvm IS code at the LLVM altitude. The substrate already had
# @code as the universal grammar-at-an-altitude discipline; this shard
# names mirror's own membership in that family.
#
# Why this matters for self-hosting (per the butterfly roadmap, Phase 2
# in `roadmap/wip/butterfly-self-hosting.md` §The compile staircase):
# when @code/mirror is the bootstrap's parser, the bootstrap stops
# being load-bearing for parsing. Mirror parses mirror through its own
# substrate-declared @code instance. The previous framing
# `@mirror/syntax` was wrong-shaped because syntax is not a sibling of
# mosaic / cli / spec / store at @mirror — syntax is what code IS at
# the mirror altitude, which means the substrate already had the word.
#
# === naming: why @code/mirror, not @mirror/code ===
#
# Two arguments converge on @code/mirror:
#
#   1. Path-namespace property (load-bearing per
#      [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]]): this file lives at
#      `shards/code/mirror.mirror` and that path declares the namespace
#      `@code/mirror`. Same shape as `shards/code/rust.mirror` declares
#      `@code/rust`. The path IS the declaration.
#
#   2. Sibling discipline: @code/mirror sits alongside @code/rust,
#      @code/gleam, @code/llvm, @code/fortran as instances of the same
#      universal discipline. Reading the family flat-namespaced makes
#      the substrate-pull recognition legible ("mirror is one of the
#      altitudes @code knows about"). @mirror/code would isolate mirror
#      as its own sub-family and lose that legibility.
#
# Alex flagged (2026-06-06) that `@X/Y/Z` namespaces may be isomorphic
# to `@Z/Y/X` because composition is order-invariant; the
# path-namespace property pulls the canonical form to the path-shape,
# which lands at @code/mirror here.
#
# === five operations at the mirror altitude ===
#
# Per the prism-as-trait-as-everything discipline, declaring @code/mirror
# IS declaring the five operations on the mirror-source manifold. The
# operation signatures inherit from @code (universal); the altitude
# specialization names what each verb does at THIS altitude. Bodies
# are abstract (the obligation block \) — the bootstrap discharges them
# today; @mirror/compile discharges them in the self-hosted phase.
#
# Spec context: docs/specs/spectral-triple-binary.md §3 (the translate
# template); roadmap/wip/butterfly-self-hosting.md §Phase 2 (parser
# self-hosting); roadmap/pending/phase-2-parser-self.md.
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#                      [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]],
#                      [[architecture-lift-as-load-bearing]].
# Related shards: code.mirror (the universal parent),
#                 code/rust.mirror (D2; the sibling precedent),
#                 code/gleam.mirror (post-migration from boot/04b),
#                 mirror/store.mirror (where @code/mirror artifacts
#                 settle as content-addressed splinters).
# Path-namespace property: this file at `shards/code/mirror.mirror`
# declares `@code/mirror` and only that.

prism @code/mirror {
  focus mirror
  project mirror
  split mirror
  shift mirror
  settle mirror
}

out @code/mirror
